' An assignment to an element of a public array field of a class, written outside the class
' (h.Values(1) = 5), crashes the compiler. The declaration of the field alone does not, and
' nor does an assignment inside the class, or the read of an element, which is refused
' (TB5033). VB6 refuses the declaration (the VB6 side is in vb6/).

Class Holder
    Public Values(1 To 3) As Long
End Class

Module Startup

    Public Sub Main()
        Dim h As New Holder
        h.Values(1) = 5
    End Sub

End Module
